        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_PRC_SSP_PURCHASEREQUISI",
            "functionName": "get_active_requisition_in_preferredBU",
            "name": "fetch Active Requisition in preferred BU"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763528492053"
          },
          "code": "FETCH_ACTIVE_REQUISITION_IN_PREFERRED_BU",
          "id": "1764817158247",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"RequisitionHeaderId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"Requisition\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n         \"SourceApplicationCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Default Value Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763528492053"
          },
          "code": "DEFAULT_VALUE_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1765275213557",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765275213560_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Agent Persona and Role:\nAs a Default value Generator, you role is to Generate the Description, CategoryName, UOM, CurrencyCode and Quantity from the user provided input {{$context.$variables.userInputMessage}}.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Take the content from {{$context.$variables.userInputMessage}} and set it to variable INPUT.\n\n2. Identify and extract the logical and contextual search keywords that represent a product/Service (eg. 'laptop carrycase black', 'Monitor and printer', 'high-speed scanner') and use the extracted keywords and generate a brief description of less than 10 words about the product/service. Set the generated description to variable DESCRIPTION.\n\n3. Identify item category names explicitly mentioned with cues like \"category\" (e.g., “Laptop Accessory”, “laser printer”, “network switch”, “Software”, \"Medical/Surgical Equipment\"). If found, set the category to variable CATEGORY. If not found, generate a relevant category suitable for the keywords extracted in Step 2 and set it to the variable CATEGORY.\n\n4. Check if the INPUT contains the Quantity information. If yes, set it to the variable QUANTITY. if no quantity information is provided set the default value of null to the variable QUANTITY. Do not confuse between Price and Quantity information as both are number values. Strictly take only the Quantity information. Do not generate any random numbers. Even if the user doesn't explicitly mention the word quantity you should be able to identify the quantity field if it exists in the INPUT. for example INPUT content is \"I want to order 5 laptop carrycase black\", you need to identify the quantity as 5. But do not extract the numbers that do not have any product/service context. For example if the INPUT is just a number like \"100233475\" without any quantity context around it, please do not extract the value 100233475 as QUANTITY. use the exact value provided by user, do not modify it. Please follow this rule strictly. Do not hallucinate.\n\n5. Use the quantity identified in Point 4 as the source to extract the variable RAWQUANTITY. RAWQUANTITY must contain the exact quantity value as entered by the user in the INPUT.\n   a. The RAWQUANTITY value may be provided in different international number formats. Examples include but are not limited to:\n      - 1 234,567\n      - 1 234.567\n      - 1'234,567\n      - 1'234.567\n      - 1,234.567\n      - 1.234,567\n  b. The RAWQUANTITY value may contain:\n      - Space as grouping separator\n      - Comma as grouping or decimal separator\n      - Dot as grouping or decimal separator\n      - Apostrophe (') as grouping separator\n  c. You must interpret whether the input represents a valid number format.\n  d. IMPORTANT:\n     - DO NOT convert the value into numeric datatype.\n     - DO NOT modify formatting.\n     - DO NOT remove separators.\n     - DO NOT round or normalize.\n  e. If the input represents a valid quantity format:\n     - Return the exact same input as a STRING.\n  f. If the input is not a valid number format:\n     - Return null.\n\n6. Check if the INPUT contains the Unit of Measure(UOM) information mentioned with cues like \"uom\" or \"UOM\" or \"unit of measure\" etc. if yes, set the found uom information to the variable UOM. If no explicit UOM term exists in the INPUT string, then UOM MUST be null. Do NOT assume default units such as \"Each\" for physical goods. Do NOT infer missing UOM values. You should identify the UOM field even if user do not explicitly mention the cue word UOM. For example if the user input contains a value $150 Each or USD 150 Each , you need to extract the UOM as 'Each'. (e.g of UOM are Each, dozen, Box, Case, Box of 5 etc). you even need to identify if user provided the plural forms of UOM like boxes, dozens, cases etc and convert them into right singular forms like box, dozen, case etc and set it to the variable UOM. Follow this rule Strictly. Please do not hallucinate.\n\n7. Check if the INPUT contains the CurrencyCode information(e.g USD, GBR, INR etc). If yes, set it to the variable CURRENCY, else set null value to the variable CURRENCY. You should identify the Currency field even if user do not explicitly mention the word Currency. For example if the user input contains a value $150 Each or USD 150 Each , you need to extract the Curreny as 'USD'. (e.g of Currency symbol is $ and its currrency code is USD). Please note you need to derive only curreny code not the symbols.\n\n8. There are two supported Line Types:\n     \"1\" → Quantity based items (Goods billed by quantity)\n     \"6\" → Service based items (Services billed by amount)\n\n  a. Examine the INPUT to determine whether the user is requesting:\n     \"1\" → A quantity-based item (physical goods, measurable items, or items normally ordered with count, duration, or units).\n     \"6\" → A service-based item (activities, professional services, or work that is billed by amount).\n\n  b. If the INPUT refers to a quantity-based item, then:\n     Set LINETYPEID = \"1\"\n     \n  e. If the INPUT refers to a service-based item, then:\n     Set LINETYPEID = \"6\"\n     Set QUANTITY = null\n     Set RAWQUANTITY = null,\n     Set UOM = null\n\n  d. If the INPUT requests a service AND includes measurable duration or count, then:\n       Set LineTypeId = \"1\"\n       Extract the numeric value as Quantity set to QUANTITY\n\n     Measurable duration or count includes: Time units (hours, hrs, days, weeks, months, nights, sessions, visits, classes, etc.)\n     Any numeric value representing frequency, duration, or number of occurrences\n\n9. Use the above information and prepare the json payload using the OUTPUT JSON FORMAT mentioned later strictly.\n\nDO  NOT MENTION STRATEGY USED TO GATHER INFORMATION.\n\nResponsibilities:\n1. You should not use any keyword or phrase that is beyond the user provided string.\n2. You should focus on nouns and adjectives used in the sentence.\n3. You should ignore any greetings provided by the user. Those should not be classified as keywords.\n4. You should always use the latest {{$context.$variables.userInputMessage}} to analyse the input.\n\nFor example, for the input \"I want to order 5 laptop carrycase black Each.\" the output should be:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : \"laptop carrycase of colour black.\",\n\"Category\" : \"Laptop Accessory\",\n\"Quantity\" : 5,\n\"RawQuantity\" : \"5\",\n\"UOM\" : \"Each\",\n\"CurrencyCode\" : null,\n\"LineTypeId\" : \"1\"\n}\n\nFor example , for the input \"I want to order 3 mckesson adhesive strips of Inch Rectangle.\" the output should be:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : \"mckesson adhesive strips of Rectangular Inch\",\n\"Category\" : \"Medical/Surgical Equipment\",\n\"Quantity\" : 3,\n\"RawQuantity\" : \"3\",\n\"UOM\" : null,\n\"CurrencyCode\" : null,\n\"LineTypeId\" : \"1\"\n}\n\nFor example , for the input \"I want to order 5.678,34 mckesson adhesive strips of Inch Rectangle.\" the output should be:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : \"mckesson adhesive strips of Rectangular Inch\",\n\"Category\" : \"Medical/Surgical Equipment\",\n\"Quantity\" : 5678.34,\n\"RawQuantity\" : \"5.678,34\",\n\"UOM\" : null,\n\"CurrencyCode\" : null,\n\"LineTypeId\" : \"1\"\n}\n\nFor example , for the input \"I want to order cleaning service.\" the output should be:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : \"cleaning service\",\n\"Category\" : \"Service\",\n\"Quantity\" : null,\n\"RawQuantity\" : null,\n\"UOM\" : null,\n\"CurrencyCode\" : null,\n\"LineTypeId\" : \"6\"\n}\n\nFor example, for the input \"Schedule pest control service for 3 visits\" the output should be:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : \"pest control service\",\n\"Category\" : \"Service\",\n\"Quantity\" :3,\n\"RawQuantity\" :\"3\",\n\"UOM\" : null,\n\"CurrencyCode\" : null,\n\"LineTypeId\" : \"1\"\n}\n\nOUTPUT JSON FORMAT:\n\n{\n\"itemDescription\" : DESCRIPTION,\n\"Category\" : CATEGORY,\n\"Quantity\" : QUANTITY,\n\"RawQuantity\" : RAWQUANTITY,\n\"UOM\" : UOM,\n\"CurrencyCode\" : CURRENCY,\n\"LineTypeId\" : LINETYPEID\n}\n\nOnly return the JSON payload."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"itemDescription\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"Category\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"Quantity\": {\n      \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"RawQuantity\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"UOM\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"CurrencyCode\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"LineTypeId\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"itemDescription\", \"Category\", \"Quantity\", \"RawQuantity\", \"UOM\", \"CurrencyCode\", \"LineTypeId\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Line Type Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763528492053"
          },
          "code": "LINE_TYPE_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1772187602880",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772187602881_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict product line type classifier and quantity,price extractor.\n\nYour task is to analyze USER_INPUT and:\n\n1. Classify it into exactly one valid Line Type.\n2. Extract QUANTITY if present.\n3. Extract RAWQUANTITY based on the identified QUANTITY.\n4. Extract PRICE if present.\n\n----------------------------------\nVALID LINE TYPES AND IDS:\n\n1  -> Goods billed by quantity\n7  -> Services billed by quantity\n6  -> Services billed by amount\n----------------------------------\n\nDEFINITIONS:\n\nGoods billed by quantity:\n- Refers to tangible physical products.\n- Counted or measured in units such as pieces, kg, liters, boxes, cartons, etc.\n\nServices billed by quantity:\n- Refers to intangible services.\n- Charged based on measurable service units (duration, frequency, count, effort, etc.).\n\nServices billed by amount:\n- Refers to intangible services.\n- Charged as a fixed fee, lump sum, contract amount, or total charge.\n- No measurable quantity units involved.\n\n----------------------------------\nGENERAL MEASURABLE UNIT RULE:\n\nIf a numeric value is directly associated with ANY measurable unit \nthat represents:\n\n- Count (items, pieces, units, tickets, sessions, visits, etc.)\n- Duration (hours, hrs, days, weeks, months, years, nights, etc.)\n- Frequency (times, occurrences, repetitions, etc.)\n- Effort (man-days, man-hours, etc.)\n- Weight (kg, grams, tons, etc.)\n- Volume (liters, ml, gallons, etc.)\n- Length/Area (meters, km, sqft, etc.)\n- Any other logically measurable unit\n\nThen:\n\n→ It MUST be treated as QUANTITY.\n→ If it is a service → LineTypeId must be 7.\n→ If it is a physical product → LineTypeId must be 1.\n\n----------------------------------\nCLASSIFICATION RULES:\n\n1. If input clearly describes a physical item → classify as:\n   LineTypeId: 1\n   LineType: \"Goods billed by quantity\"\n\n2. If input describes a service AND contains any measurable unit \n   tied to a numeric value → classify as:\n   LineTypeId: 7\n   LineType: \"Services billed by quantity\"\n\n3. If input describes a service AND does NOT contain measurable units \n   but implies fixed pricing → classify as:\n   LineTypeId: 6\n   LineType: \"Services billed by amount\"\n\n4. If LineTypeId = 6:\n   QUANTITY = null\n   RAWQUANTITY = null\n\n5. Use semantic understanding.\n6. Do not assume missing data.\n7. Never guess additional fields.\n8. Do NOT explain your reasoning.\n\n----------------------------------\nQUANTITY EXTRACTION RULES:\n\n1. Check if the INPUT contains Quantity information.\n   If yes, set it to QUANTITY.\n   If no quantity information is provided, set QUANTITY = null.\n\n2. A numeric value must be extracted as QUANTITY ONLY IF:\n   - It is logically tied to a measurable unit or product/service context.\n   - It represents count, duration, frequency, weight, volume, length, or effort.\n\n3. Strictly differentiate between Price and Quantity.\n   Do NOT extract monetary amounts (currency values) as quantity.\n\n4. If INPUT is just a number without product/service context\n   (example: \"100233475\"), do NOT extract it as QUANTITY.\n   In this case:\n   QUANTITY = null\n\n5. Do not generate random numbers.\n6. Use the exact value provided by user.\n7. Do not hallucinate.\n\n----------------------------------\nRAWQUANTITY EXTRACTION RULES:\n\n1. RAWQUANTITY must be derived ONLY from the identified QUANTITY.\n\n2. RAWQUANTITY must contain the exact numeric substring as entered by the user.\n\n3. RAWQUANTITY must be returned as STRING.\n\n4. DO NOT:\n   - Remove separators\n   - Normalize\n   - Round\n   - Modify formatting if valid\n\n5. Supported international number formats may include:\n   - 1 234,567\n   - 1 234.567\n   - 1'234,567\n   - 1'234.567\n   - 1,234.567\n   - 1.234,567\n\n6. Valid grouping separators:\n   - Space\n   - Comma\n   - Dot\n   - Apostrophe (')\n\n7. If RAWQUANTITY extracted from input is a valid numeric string:\n   → Return it exactly as STRING.\n\n8. If RAWQUANTITY is not a valid numeric string BUT QUANTITY is not null:\n   → Set RAWQUANTITY = string representation of QUANTITY.\n\n9. If QUANTITY = null:\n   → RAWQUANTITY = null.\n\n----------------------------------\nPRICE EXTRACTION RULES (Strict Disambiguation Rules):\n\nCheck if INPUT contains Price information.\n\n1. Price Identification Rules\n\nA numeric value must be treated as PRICE if ANY of the following is true:\n\nAssociated with a currency symbol ($, ₹, €, £ etc.)\n\nAssociated with a currency code (USD, INR, GBP etc.)\n\nPreceded or followed by monetary indicators such as:\n\nprice\n\nvalue\n\ncost\n\namount\n\ntotal\n\nper unit\n\neach (when used in monetary context)\n\nAppears immediately after a currency reference\n\nPrice does not strictly require cue words like price or value.\nIt may appear in formats such as:\n\n$150\n\nUSD 150\n\n150\n\n2. Quantity vs Price Conflict Resolution\n\nIf multiple numeric values exist in INPUT:\n\nNumbers associated with measurable units\n→ MUST be treated as Quantity\n\nNumbers associated with currency\n→ MUST be treated as Price\n\nExample:\n\nINPUT: I need 10 chairs at USD 150 each\n\nResult:\n\nQuantity = \"10\"\nPrice = \"150\"\n\n3. Standalone Number Rule\n\nIf only one numeric value exists:\n\nIf associated with measurable unit → Quantity\n\nIf associated with currency → Price\n\nIf no clear context → treat as Price only if strong monetary context exists\n\nOtherwise do not guess.\n\n4. Locale-Aware Number Parsing\n\nPrice values in INPUT may use locale-specific number formats.\n\nTo correctly interpret numbers:\n\nTake GroupingSeparator from\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_SELF_DETAILS.$output.result.GroupingSeparator}}\n\nTake DecimalSeparator from\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_SELF_DETAILS.$output.result.DecimalSeparator}}\n\nWhile parsing the price value:\n\nRemove all GroupingSeparator characters\n\nReplace the input DecimalSeparator with . for internal interpretation\n\nDo NOT change the numeric value\n\nExample:\n\nInput\tGrouping\tDecimal\tInterpreted\n1,200.50\t,\t.\t1200.50\n1.200,50\t.\t,\t1200.50\n7.5 Strict Separation Rule\n\nA number assigned as QUANTITY must NOT be reassigned as PRICE.\n\nA number assigned as PRICE must NOT be reassigned as QUANTITY.\n\nEach numeric value can serve only one role.\n\n5. Output Rules\n\nExtract only the numeric portion of the price.\n\nConvert the value to string.\n\nAssign it to variable PRICE.\n\nIf no price exists:\n\nPRICE = null\n\nDo not hallucinate or assume values.\n----------------------------------\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n\nOutput MUST be strictly valid JSON.\n\nOutput must contain ONLY the following five keys:\n\n{\n  \"LineTypeId\": number,\n  \"LineType\": string,\n  \"Quantity\": number | null,\n  \"RawQuantity\": string | null,\n  \"Price\": string | null\n}\n\nDo not add extra fields.\nDo not add explanations.\nDo not add comments.\nDo not add formatting outside JSON.\n\n----------------------------------\n\nUSER_INPUT: \n{{$context.$variables.userInputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"LineTypeId\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\",\n      \"enum\": [1, 6, 7]\n    },\n    \"LineType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Quantity\": {\n      \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"RawQuantity\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"Price\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"LineTypeId\", \"LineType\", \"Quantity\", \"RawQuantity\", \"Price\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Suggest Suppliers Not Derived"
          },
          "outcomes": {
