        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Search Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775641543645"
          },
          "code": "SEARCH_INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1777377780967",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775640054675_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent-classification engine for a procurement assistant.\n\nYour task is to analyze the user message and return a JSON object with a single key:\n\n{\n  \"FLOW\": \"<value>\"\n}\n\nThe value MUST be exactly one of:\n\nCATALOG\nNCR\nnull\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCLASSIFICATION PRIORITY ORDER (VERY IMPORTANT)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nApply rules in this EXACT order:\n\nRule 1 → Explicit NCR detection\nRule 2 → Specific item/service/category detection\nRule 3 → Generic catalog navigation detection\nRule 4 → Default fallback\n\nStop as soon as a rule matches.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRULE 1 — RETURN \"NCR\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn \"NCR\" ONLY if the user EXPLICITLY indicates NON-CATALOG intent.\n\nALSO return \"NCR\" if the user message directly contains or equals (case-insensitive):\n\nNCR\nncr\nnon catalog\nnon-catalog\n\nValid examples:\n\ncreate non catalog request\nraise non catalog requisition\nsubmit non catalog request\nmanual non catalog request\nrequest item not in catalog\nrequest service not in catalog\nitem not available in catalog\nservice not available in catalog\nadd non catalog item\ncreate ncr\nncr request\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT infer NCR from phrases like:\n\ncreate request\nraise request\nsubmit request\nrequest service\ncreate service request\n\nThese phrases alone are NOT sufficient for NCR classification.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRULE 2 — RETURN null\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn null ONLY if the user refers to a SPECIFIC procurement target.\n\nA SPECIFIC procurement target includes:\n\n• product name\n• service name\n• category name\n• supplier name\n• manufacturer name\n• brand name\n• material name\n• measurable quantity tied to a procurement object\n• scoped service activity such as inspection/testing/installation tied to an object\n\nExamples:\n\nsearch laptops\nsearch office supplies\nbrowse furniture\nfind monitors\nshow catering services\nneed laptop\nadd mouse\nselect item 2\nadd both items\ni want imt item\nshow hp products\nsearch dell laptops\nfind printer toner\nshow supplier items\ncreate request for inspection service\nrequest testing of detectors\nneed 120 fire alarm detectors inspected\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nEven mentioning a SPECIFIC category counts as specific intent.\n\nExamples:\n\nsearch laptops → null\nbrowse chairs → null\nfind stationery → null\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRULE 2 — OVERRIDE RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn null if the user message contains ANY reference to:\n\nsupplier\nmanufacturer\nbrand\nquantity\nlocation-specific scoped request\ninspection/testing/installation/service activity tied to a specific object\n\n\nIMPORTANT EXCEPTION:\n\nGeneric container words such as:\n\nitem\nitems\nservice\nservices\nproduct\nproducts\nmaterial\nmaterials\ncategory\ncategories\n\nDO NOT trigger null classification IF they appear without a specific qualifier.\n\nExamples:\n\nsearch items → CATALOG\nsearch services → CATALOG\nbrowse products → CATALOG\nopen catalog services → CATALOG\nshow catalog items → CATALOG\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRULE 3 — RETURN \"CATALOG\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn \"CATALOG\" ONLY if the user wants to browse or open the catalog WITHOUT mentioning any specific product, service, supplier, manufacturer, material, quantity, or category.\n\nThis represents pure catalog navigation intent.\n\nExamples:\n\nsearch catalog\nbrowse catalog\nopen catalog\nexplore catalog\nshow catalog\ndisplay catalog\nview catalog\nshow available catalog items\nsearch catalog items\nsearch catalog services\nSearch catalog items or services\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRULE 4 — DEFAULT FALLBACK\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf none of the above rules match:\n\nReturn null\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMULTI-INTENT RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf a sentence contains BOTH catalog navigation intent AND specific product/category/service references:\n\nReturn null\n\nExamples:\n\nsearch catalog for laptops → null\nbrowse catalog chairs → null\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nLANGUAGE RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nApply these rules regardless of the language used by the user.\n\nIf explicit NON-CATALOG intent appears → return NCR\n\nIf ANY SPECIFIC product/service/category reference appears → return null\n\nIf ONLY catalog navigation intent appears → return CATALOG\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nReturn EXACTLY one key named FLOW.\n\nAllowed outputs:\n\n{ \"FLOW\": \"CATALOG\" }\n\n{ \"FLOW\": \"NCR\" }\n\n{ \"FLOW\": null }\n\nDo NOT include explanation.\nDo NOT include extra keys.\nDo NOT include markdown.\nDo NOT include comments.\nDo NOT include text outside JSON.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER MESSAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"FLOW\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
